Running #VSLAM on your own #iPhone #RGBD Recordings

🎬 Video: https://youtu.be/mLIFRiAxRs4
🔗 VSLAM-LAB: https://lnkd.in/gGZifSb3
🔗 AllFeature-VSLAM: https://lnkd.in/gRztKMHT

Using the Stray Scanner App, I recorded an RGB-D dataset at Old Parliament House, straight from a LiDAR-enabled iPhone. The app gives direct access to the raw RGB-D video it captures, and outputs a simple .zip file with your data.

One command converts that recording into the VSLAM-LAB format (rgb, depth, intrinsics, poses). From that point, every system available in VSLAM-LAB runs on your footage with zero additional effort — MASt3R-SLAM, DROID-SLAM, DPVO, VGGT-SLAM, COLMAP, AllFeature-VSLAM ...:

pixi run demo orbslam3 strayscanner old_parliament_house rgbd

You can also interactively visualise any VSLAM-LAB dataset:

pixi run rerun-vis eth table_3

🎬 Video: https://youtu.be/wbtJo3ZHWH0

The gap between "I just filmed something" and "I have SLAM results  is now one command.

